---
description: "Error handling conventions for API routes, server actions, and client mutations"
globs: ["app/**/route.ts", "app/**/actions.ts", "lib/hooks/**/*.ts"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# Error handling

- API routes/server actions throw typed errors (`ForbiddenError`,
  `NotFoundError`, `ValidationError`) caught by a single error-mapping
  layer that converts them to HTTP status codes. Don't hand-roll
  `res.status(x)` inline in every handler.
- Never expose internal error messages, stack traces, or DB errors to the
  client response — log server-side, return a generic message client-side.
- Client-side mutations (React Query) always handle the error state in the
  UI — no silent failures. A failed renewal, invite, or grant request must
  surface a visible message to the Admin.
- Validation errors from zod are mapped field-by-field back to the form
  (react-hook-form), not shown as one generic toast.
- After writing a new API route, verify: does every failure path return a
  typed error, and does the caller actually handle it (not just `.catch(() => {})`)?
